{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0141PFuh1L1eMm4qnqVkZdm4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t# hr-helpdesk-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\n     4\tshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\n     5\tthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Components\n     8\t\n     9\t| Component | Code | Identity |\n    10\t|---|---|---|\n    11\t| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n    12\t| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n    13\t| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n    14\t| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n    15\t| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n    16\t\n    17\t## How a request flows\n    18\t\n    19\t1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n    20\t   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n    21\t2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n    22\t   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n    23\t3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n    24\t   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n    25\t   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n    26\t   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n    27\t4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n    28\t   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n    29\t   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n    30\t   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n    31\t5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n    32\t   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n    33\t6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n    34\t   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n    35\t\n    36\tEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n    37\t\n    38\t## Stopping the agent\n    39\t\n    40\tOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n    41\t\n    42\t```sql\n    43\tINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n    44\t-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\tRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\n    48\tcalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\n    49\tLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Audit retention\n    52\t\n    53\tAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\n    54\tPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n    55\t`hr_audit_reader`.\n    56\t\n    57\t## Releases\n    58\t\n    59\tMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n    60\t`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\n    61\trecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\n    62\tdiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\n    63\tworkflow from `main`.\n     1\tapiVersion: batch/v1\n     2\tkind: CronJob\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: audit-partition-maintenance\n     5\t  namespace: hr-agent\n     6\t  labels: {app.kubernetes.io/part-of: hr-helpdesk}\n     7\tspec:\n     8\t  schedule: \"17 2 * * *\"\n     9\t  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n    10\t  jobTemplate:\n    11\t    spec:\n    12\t      backoffLimit: 2\n    13\t      template:\n    14\t        metadata:\n    15\t          labels: {app: audit-maintenance}\n    16\t        spec:\n    17\t          serviceAccountName: hr-audit-maint\n    18\t          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n    19\t          restartPolicy: OnFailure\n    20\t          securityContext:\n    21\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n    22\t            runAsUser: 70\n    23\t            seccompProfile: {type: RuntimeDefault}\n    24\t          containers:\n    25\t            - name: maintain\n    26\t              image: registry.acme.example/platform/psql@sha256:9b2e61c04d7f3a85e1c6b09d2f4a7e3c58d1b6a0f9e2c47d3b8a15e6f0c9d2a4\n    27\t              env:\n    28\t                - name: PGSERVICE\n    29\t                  value: hr_audit_maint\n    30\t                - name: PERIOD\n    31\t                  value: \"1 week\"\n    32\t                - name: AHEAD\n    33\t                  value: \"4\"\n    34\t                - name: KEEP_PARTITIONS\n    35\t                  value: \"6\"\n    36\t              command: [\"psql\", \"-v\", \"ON_ERROR_STOP=1\", \"-c\"]\n    37\t              args:\n    38\t                - >-\n    39\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.events', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    40\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.gateway_decisions', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    41\t              securityContext:\n    42\t                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    43\t                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n    44\t                capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\n    45\t              volumeMounts:\n    46\t                - {name: pgservice, mountPath: /etc/postgresql-common, readOnly: true}\n    47\t          volumes:\n    48\t            - name: pgservice\n    49\t              secret: {secretName: hr-audit-maint-pgservice}\n     1\t-- Roles (created by the platform team): hr_agent, hr_gateway, hr_agent_operator,\n     2\t-- hr_audit_reader, hr_audit_maint, hr_docs_ingest.\n     3\tCREATE SCHEMA audit; CREATE SCHEMA control; CREATE SCHEMA approvals; CREATE SCHEMA quota; CREATE SCHEMA retrieval;\n     4\t\n     5\tCREATE TABLE audit.events (\n     6\t    event_id uuid NOT NULL, ts timestamptz NOT NULL, event_type text NOT NULL,\n     7\t    run_id uuid NOT NULL, step_id uuid, parent_step_id uuid,\n     8\t    accountable_party text NOT NULL, operational_owner text NOT NULL, tenant text NOT NULL,\n     9\t    agent_type_id text NOT NULL, agent_instance_id text NOT NULL,\n    10\t    trace_id char(32) NOT NULL, span_id char(16) NOT NULL, traceparent text NOT NULL,\n    11\t    delegated_subject text NOT NULL, agent_principal text NOT NULL,\n    12\t    tool text, operation_target text, decision text, reason text, policy_version text NOT NULL, approval_id uuid,\n    13\t    args_redacted jsonb, result_redacted jsonb,\n    14\t    context_tokens integer, context_tokens_method text, model_requested text, model_served text,\n    15\t    PRIMARY KEY (event_id, ts)\n    16\t) PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);\n    17\tCREATE INDEX ON audit.events (trace_id);\n    18\tCREATE INDEX ON audit.events (run_id, ts);\n    19\t\n    20\tCREATE TABLE audit.gateway_decisions (\n    21\t    ts timestamptz NOT NULL, traceparent text NOT NULL, tenant text NOT NULL,\n    22\t    accountable_party text NOT NULL, operational_owner text NOT NULL,\n    23\t    agent_type_id_hint text NOT NULL, agent_instance_hint text NOT NULL,   -- caller-supplied; join key only\n    24\t    subject text, actor text, tool text, decision text NOT NULL, reason text, policy_version text NOT NULL\n    25\t) PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);\n    26\t\n    27\t-- Creates `ahead` partitions into the future and drops partitions older than the newest `keep`.\n    28\tCREATE FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(parent regclass, period interval, ahead int, keep int)\n    29\tRETURNS void LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = audit, pg_temp AS $$\n    30\tDECLARE\n    31\t    start_ts timestamptz := date_trunc('week', now());\n    32\t    part record;\n    33\tBEGIN\n    34\t    FOR i IN 0..ahead LOOP\n    35\t        EXECUTE format('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s_%s PARTITION OF %s FOR VALUES FROM (%L) TO (%L)',\n    36\t                       parent, to_char(start_ts + i * period, 'IYYY\"w\"IW'), parent,\n    37\t                       start_ts + i * period, start_ts + (i + 1) * period);\n    38\t    END LOOP;\n    39\t    FOR part IN\n    40\t        SELECT c.oid::regclass AS rel FROM pg_inherits i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.inhrelid\n    41\t         WHERE i.inhparent = parent ORDER BY c.relname DESC OFFSET keep + ahead + 1\n    42\t    LOOP\n    43\t        EXECUTE format('DROP TABLE %s', part.rel);\n    44\t    END LOOP;\n    45\tEND $$;\n    46\t\n    47\tCREATE TABLE control.stop_flags (\n    48\t    flag_id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,\n    49\t    scope text NOT NULL CHECK (scope IN ('fleet', 'agent_type', 'agent_instance', 'subject', 'agent_principal')),\n    50\t    value text, active boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true, reason text NOT NULL,\n    51\t    set_by text NOT NULL DEFAULT current_user, set_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n    52\t);\n    53\t\n    54\tCREATE TABLE approvals.grants (\n    55\t    approval_id uuid PRIMARY KEY, run_id uuid NOT NULL, agent_instance_id text NOT NULL, subject text NOT NULL,\n    56\t    operation text NOT NULL, target text NOT NULL, args_sha256 char(64) NOT NULL, args jsonb NOT NULL,\n    57\t    tool_use_id text NOT NULL, description text NOT NULL,\n    58\t    requested_at timestamptz NOT NULL, expires_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    59\t    approved_by text, approved_at timestamptz, used_at timestamptz\n    60\t);\n    61\t\n    62\tCREATE TABLE quota.usage (\n    63\t    scope text NOT NULL, key text NOT NULL, window_start timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    64\t    runs integer NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, tokens bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, cost_usd numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    65\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, window_start)\n    66\t);\n    67\t\n    68\tCREATE TABLE retrieval.index_state (id int PRIMARY KEY CHECK (id = 1), version text NOT NULL);\n    69\tCREATE TABLE retrieval.chunks (\n    70\t    chunk_id text PRIMARY KEY, doc_id text NOT NULL, source text NOT NULL,\n    71\t    added_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(), added_by text NOT NULL DEFAULT current_user,\n    72\t    trust text NOT NULL CHECK (trust IN ('reviewed', 'hr_authored')),\n    73\t    audience text NOT NULL CHECK (audience IN ('all', 'employee')),\n    74\t    allowed_employees text[] NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n    75\t    expires_at timestamptz, quarantined boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false, text text NOT NULL,\n    76\t    tsv tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS (to_tsvector('english', text)) STORED\n    77\t);\n    78\tCREATE INDEX ON retrieval.chunks USING gin (tsv);\n    79\t\n    80\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit, control, approvals, quota, retrieval TO hr_agent;\n    81\tGRANT INSERT ON audit.events TO hr_agent;\n    82\tGRANT SELECT ON control.stop_flags TO hr_agent;\n    83\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON approvals.grants TO hr_agent;\n    84\tGRANT UPDATE (approved_by, approved_at, used_at) ON approvals.grants TO hr_agent;\n    85\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON quota.usage TO hr_agent;\n    86\tGRANT SELECT ON retrieval.chunks, retrieval.index_state TO hr_agent;\n    87\t\n    88\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit, control TO hr_gateway;\n    89\tGRANT INSERT ON audit.gateway_decisions TO hr_gateway;\n    90\tGRANT SELECT ON control.stop_flags TO hr_gateway;\n    91\t\n    92\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA control TO hr_agent_operator;\n    93\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control.stop_flags TO hr_agent_operator;\n    94\tGRANT USAGE ON SEQUENCE control.stop_flags_flag_id_seq TO hr_agent_operator;\n    95\t\n    96\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit TO hr_audit_reader, hr_audit_maint;\n    97\tGRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA audit TO hr_audit_reader;\n    98\tREVOKE EXECUTE ON FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(regclass, interval, int, int) FROM PUBLIC;\n    99\tGRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(regclass, interval, int, int) TO hr_audit_maint;\n   100\t\n   101\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA retrieval TO hr_docs_ingest;\n   102\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON retrieval.chunks, retrieval.index_state TO hr_docs_ingest;\n     1\t\"\"\"Checks applied to content before the model sees it, and to model output.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport json\n     5\timport re\n     6\timport unicodedata\n     7\tfrom typing import Any\n     8\tfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n     9\t\n    10\tfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom .redact import redact_obj\n    13\tfrom .tools import ToolSpec\n    14\t\n    15\t_INJECTION_MARKERS = [\n    16\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\bignore (all|any|the)? ?(previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    17\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are now\\b\"),\n    18\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\bsystem prompt\\b\"),\n    19\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)<\\s*/?\\s*(system|assistant|tool_use|instructions)\\b\"),\n    20\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) the [a-z_]+ tool\\b\"),\n    21\t    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n    22\t]\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass ValidationRejected(Exception):\n    26\t    def __init__(self, reason: str):\n    27\t        super().__init__(reason)\n    28\t        self.reason = reason\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef _scan_text(value: str, where: str) -> None:\n    32\t    for ch in value:\n    33\t        cat = unicodedata.category(ch)\n    34\t        if cat in (\"Cf\", \"Co\", \"Cs\") or (cat == \"Cc\" and ch not in \"\\n\\t\"):\n    35\t            raise ValidationRejected(f\"{where}: control or invisible character\")\n    36\t    for marker in _INJECTION_MARKERS:\n    37\t        if marker.search(value):\n    38\t            raise ValidationRejected(f\"{where}: instruction-like content\")\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef _walk_strings(value: Any, where: str) -> None:\n    42\t    if isinstance(value, str):\n    43\t        _scan_text(value, where)\n    44\t    elif isinstance(value, dict):\n    45\t        for k, v in value.items():\n    46\t            _walk_strings(v, f\"{where}.{k}\")\n    47\t    elif isinstance(value, list):\n    48\t        for i, v in enumerate(value):\n    49\t            _walk_strings(v, f\"{where}[{i}]\")\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef validate_tool_args(spec: ToolSpec, args: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    53\t    if not isinstance(args, dict):\n    54\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"arguments must be an object\")\n    55\t    errors = sorted(Draft202012Validator(spec.input_schema, format_checker=FormatChecker()).iter_errors(args), key=str)\n    56\t    if errors:\n    57\t        raise ValidationRejected(f\"argument schema: {errors[0].message}\")\n    58\t    return args\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef validate_tool_output(spec: ToolSpec, payload: Any, max_bytes: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    62\t    \"\"\"Type, size, schema and content checks. Any failure rejects the payload.\"\"\"\n    63\t    if spec.output_schema is None:\n    64\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"no output schema configured\")\n    65\t    encoded = json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)\n    66\t    if len(encoded.encode()) > max_bytes:\n    67\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"output too large\")\n    68\t    if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n    69\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"output must be an object\")\n    70\t    errors = list(Draft202012Validator(spec.output_schema, format_checker=FormatChecker()).iter_errors(payload))\n    71\t    if errors:\n    72\t        raise ValidationRejected(f\"output schema: {errors[0].message}\")\n    73\t    _walk_strings(payload, spec.qualified)\n    74\t    return redact_obj(payload)\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef validate_chunk(chunk: dict[str, Any], max_chars: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    78\t    text = chunk[\"text\"]\n    79\t    if not isinstance(text, str) or len(text) > max_chars:\n    80\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"chunk size\")\n    81\t    _walk_strings(text, f\"chunk:{chunk['chunk_id']}\")\n    82\t    return {\n    83\t        \"chunk_id\": chunk[\"chunk_id\"],\n    84\t        \"source\": chunk[\"source\"],\n    85\t        \"trust\": chunk[\"trust\"],\n    86\t        \"text\": redact_obj(text),\n    87\t    }\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t_MD_IMAGE = re.compile(r\"!\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\([^)]*\\)\")\n    91\t_MD_LINK = re.compile(r\"\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)[^)]*\\)\")\n    92\t_BARE_URL = re.compile(r\"https?://[^\\s)>\\]]+\")\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tdef sanitize_reply(text: str, allowed_hosts: list[str]) -> str:\n    96\t    \"\"\"Strip images and links to hosts outside the allowlist before the chat client renders them.\"\"\"\n    97\t    text = _MD_IMAGE.sub(\"[image removed]\", text)\n    98\t\n    99\t    def _link(m: re.Match[str]) -> str:\n   100\t        host = urlparse(m.group(2)).hostname or \"\"\n   101\t        return m.group(0) if host in allowed_hosts else m.group(1)\n   102\t\n   103\t    text = _MD_LINK.sub(_link, text)\n   104\t\n   105\t    def _bare(m: re.Match[str]) -> str:\n   106\t        host = urlparse(m.group(0)).hostname or \"\"\n   107\t        return m.group(0) if host in allowed_hosts else \"[link removed]\"\n   108\t\n   109\t    return _BARE_URL.sub(_bare, text)\nsrc/credentials.py:68:    def drop_subject(self, subject: str) -> None:\nk8s/deployment.yaml:60:            capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nk8s/deployment.yaml:113:            capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nk8s/audit-maintenance.yaml:44:                capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nrelease/manifest.yaml:79:  retention: 6 months","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca543b1a-4cf7-4416-b4c0-b3437adb0361","uuid":"4bfeb050-b6c4-4dcf-ae74-afd1b8c4b125","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:22:40.242Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t# hr-helpdesk-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tAn HR helpdesk assistant for Acme employees. It answers policy questions from the HR handbook,\n     4\tshows the signed-in employee their own leave balance, files leave requests (the manager approves\n     5\tthem in HRIS), and hands conversations to an HR advisor.\n     6\t\n     7\t## Components\n     8\t\n     9\t| Component | Code | Identity |\n    10\t|---|---|---|\n    11\t| Agent API and loop | `src/main.py`, `src/agent.py` | SA `hr-helpdesk-agent`, SPIFFE SVID |\n    12\t| Tool gateway | `src/gateway.py` | SA `hr-tool-gateway` |\n    13\t| HRIS MCP server | owned by hris-platform | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/hris/sa/hris-mcp` |\n    14\t| Helpdesk MCP server | owned by it-service-desk | `spiffe://acme.example/ns/helpdesk/sa/helpdesk-mcp` |\n    15\t| Audit, approvals, quotas, stop flags, handbook index | Postgres (`migrations/001_init.sql`) | per-component DB roles |\n    16\t\n    17\t## How a request flows\n    18\t\n    19\t1. The HR portal sends the employee's SSO token. `main.py` verifies issuer, audience, expiry and\n    20\t   organisation; the employee id and tenant come only from that token.\n    21\t2. The loop (`agent.py`) checks the stop flags and the run budget before every model call, and\n    22\t   records usage against per-user, tenant and fleet quotas.\n    23\t3. Tool calls are looked up by exact name in `config/tools.yaml`. Arguments are schema-checked.\n    24\t   `file_leave_request` and `escalate_to_human` pause the run and show the employee exactly what\n    25\t   will be sent; the approval is bound to the run instance, operation, target and argument hash,\n    26\t   expires after 10 minutes, and is consumed once.\n    27\t4. MCP calls go to the gateway with a 300-second token for that one tool scope, minted by STS\n    28\t   from the agent's workload identity and the employee's token. The gateway verifies the token\n    29\t   and its certificate binding, checks scope, stop flags, rate limits and argument schema, swaps\n    30\t   the token for one addressed to the MCP server, and validates the response schema.\n    31\t5. Tool output is size-, schema- and content-checked and redacted before the model sees it.\n    32\t   Handbook passages are filtered at query time to documents the employee may see.\n    33\t6. Every step writes an `audit.events` row with the six identity fields and trace context.\n    34\t   If the audit write fails, the run stops.\n    35\t\n    36\tEscalations are delivered even during gateway maintenance windows.\n    37\t\n    38\t## Stopping the agent\n    39\t\n    40\tOperators with the `hr_agent_operator` DB role insert into `control.stop_flags`:\n    41\t\n    42\t```sql\n    43\tINSERT INTO control.stop_flags (scope, value, reason) VALUES ('fleet', NULL, 'incident 2291');\n    44\t-- or scope 'agent_type' / 'agent_instance' / 'subject' / 'agent_principal'\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\tRunning agents see the flag within 2 seconds and cancel in-flight work; the gateway refuses\n    48\tcalls immediately. Target stop time: 10 seconds. The agent's DB role can only read this table.\n    49\tLast drill: see `docs/drills/` in the ops repo.\n    50\t\n    51\t## Audit retention\n    52\t\n    53\tAudit records are kept for six months (Acme records policy; employment-related AI use in the EU).\n    54\tPartitions are created and dropped nightly by `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml`. Access is limited to\n    55\t`hr_audit_reader`.\n    56\t\n    57\t## Releases\n    58\t\n    59\tMerges to `main` build, sign and attest the image, compute the agent-type-id over every file in\n    60\t`src/`, `prompts/`, `config/`, plus `requirements.txt`, `Dockerfile`, the image digest and the model\n    61\trecord, and stamp `release/manifest.yaml`. Pods refuse to start if the type id they compute\n    62\tdiffers from the one they were deployed with. Kyverno admits only signed images built by this\n    63\tworkflow from `main`.\n     1\tapiVersion: batch/v1\n     2\tkind: CronJob\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: audit-partition-maintenance\n     5\t  namespace: hr-agent\n     6\t  labels: {app.kubernetes.io/part-of: hr-helpdesk}\n     7\tspec:\n     8\t  schedule: \"17 2 * * *\"\n     9\t  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n    10\t  jobTemplate:\n    11\t    spec:\n    12\t      backoffLimit: 2\n    13\t      template:\n    14\t        metadata:\n    15\t          labels: {app: audit-maintenance}\n    16\t        spec:\n    17\t          serviceAccountName: hr-audit-maint\n    18\t          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n    19\t          restartPolicy: OnFailure\n    20\t          securityContext:\n    21\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n    22\t            runAsUser: 70\n    23\t            seccompProfile: {type: RuntimeDefault}\n    24\t          containers:\n    25\t            - name: maintain\n    26\t              image: registry.acme.example/platform/psql@sha256:9b2e61c04d7f3a85e1c6b09d2f4a7e3c58d1b6a0f9e2c47d3b8a15e6f0c9d2a4\n    27\t              env:\n    28\t                - name: PGSERVICE\n    29\t                  value: hr_audit_maint\n    30\t                - name: PERIOD\n    31\t                  value: \"1 week\"\n    32\t                - name: AHEAD\n    33\t                  value: \"4\"\n    34\t                - name: KEEP_PARTITIONS\n    35\t                  value: \"6\"\n    36\t              command: [\"psql\", \"-v\", \"ON_ERROR_STOP=1\", \"-c\"]\n    37\t              args:\n    38\t                - >-\n    39\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.events', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    40\t                  SELECT audit.maintain_partitions('audit.gateway_decisions', '$(PERIOD)', $(AHEAD), $(KEEP_PARTITIONS));\n    41\t              securityContext:\n    42\t                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    43\t                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n    44\t                capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\n    45\t              volumeMounts:\n    46\t                - {name: pgservice, mountPath: /etc/postgresql-common, readOnly: true}\n    47\t          volumes:\n    48\t            - name: pgservice\n    49\t              secret: {secretName: hr-audit-maint-pgservice}\n     1\t-- Roles (created by the platform team): hr_agent, hr_gateway, hr_agent_operator,\n     2\t-- hr_audit_reader, hr_audit_maint, hr_docs_ingest.\n     3\tCREATE SCHEMA audit; CREATE SCHEMA control; CREATE SCHEMA approvals; CREATE SCHEMA quota; CREATE SCHEMA retrieval;\n     4\t\n     5\tCREATE TABLE audit.events (\n     6\t    event_id uuid NOT NULL, ts timestamptz NOT NULL, event_type text NOT NULL,\n     7\t    run_id uuid NOT NULL, step_id uuid, parent_step_id uuid,\n     8\t    accountable_party text NOT NULL, operational_owner text NOT NULL, tenant text NOT NULL,\n     9\t    agent_type_id text NOT NULL, agent_instance_id text NOT NULL,\n    10\t    trace_id char(32) NOT NULL, span_id char(16) NOT NULL, traceparent text NOT NULL,\n    11\t    delegated_subject text NOT NULL, agent_principal text NOT NULL,\n    12\t    tool text, operation_target text, decision text, reason text, policy_version text NOT NULL, approval_id uuid,\n    13\t    args_redacted jsonb, result_redacted jsonb,\n    14\t    context_tokens integer, context_tokens_method text, model_requested text, model_served text,\n    15\t    PRIMARY KEY (event_id, ts)\n    16\t) PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);\n    17\tCREATE INDEX ON audit.events (trace_id);\n    18\tCREATE INDEX ON audit.events (run_id, ts);\n    19\t\n    20\tCREATE TABLE audit.gateway_decisions (\n    21\t    ts timestamptz NOT NULL, traceparent text NOT NULL, tenant text NOT NULL,\n    22\t    accountable_party text NOT NULL, operational_owner text NOT NULL,\n    23\t    agent_type_id_hint text NOT NULL, agent_instance_hint text NOT NULL,   -- caller-supplied; join key only\n    24\t    subject text, actor text, tool text, decision text NOT NULL, reason text, policy_version text NOT NULL\n    25\t) PARTITION BY RANGE (ts);\n    26\t\n    27\t-- Creates `ahead` partitions into the future and drops partitions older than the newest `keep`.\n    28\tCREATE FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(parent regclass, period interval, ahead int, keep int)\n    29\tRETURNS void LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER SET search_path = audit, pg_temp AS $$\n    30\tDECLARE\n    31\t    start_ts timestamptz := date_trunc('week', now());\n    32\t    part record;\n    33\tBEGIN\n    34\t    FOR i IN 0..ahead LOOP\n    35\t        EXECUTE format('CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS %s_%s PARTITION OF %s FOR VALUES FROM (%L) TO (%L)',\n    36\t                       parent, to_char(start_ts + i * period, 'IYYY\"w\"IW'), parent,\n    37\t                       start_ts + i * period, start_ts + (i + 1) * period);\n    38\t    END LOOP;\n    39\t    FOR part IN\n    40\t        SELECT c.oid::regclass AS rel FROM pg_inherits i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.inhrelid\n    41\t         WHERE i.inhparent = parent ORDER BY c.relname DESC OFFSET keep + ahead + 1\n    42\t    LOOP\n    43\t        EXECUTE format('DROP TABLE %s', part.rel);\n    44\t    END LOOP;\n    45\tEND $$;\n    46\t\n    47\tCREATE TABLE control.stop_flags (\n    48\t    flag_id bigserial PRIMARY KEY,\n    49\t    scope text NOT NULL CHECK (scope IN ('fleet', 'agent_type', 'agent_instance', 'subject', 'agent_principal')),\n    50\t    value text, active boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT true, reason text NOT NULL,\n    51\t    set_by text NOT NULL DEFAULT current_user, set_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now()\n    52\t);\n    53\t\n    54\tCREATE TABLE approvals.grants (\n    55\t    approval_id uuid PRIMARY KEY, run_id uuid NOT NULL, agent_instance_id text NOT NULL, subject text NOT NULL,\n    56\t    operation text NOT NULL, target text NOT NULL, args_sha256 char(64) NOT NULL, args jsonb NOT NULL,\n    57\t    tool_use_id text NOT NULL, description text NOT NULL,\n    58\t    requested_at timestamptz NOT NULL, expires_at timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    59\t    approved_by text, approved_at timestamptz, used_at timestamptz\n    60\t);\n    61\t\n    62\tCREATE TABLE quota.usage (\n    63\t    scope text NOT NULL, key text NOT NULL, window_start timestamptz NOT NULL,\n    64\t    runs integer NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, tokens bigint NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, cost_usd numeric(12, 4) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n    65\t    PRIMARY KEY (scope, key, window_start)\n    66\t);\n    67\t\n    68\tCREATE TABLE retrieval.index_state (id int PRIMARY KEY CHECK (id = 1), version text NOT NULL);\n    69\tCREATE TABLE retrieval.chunks (\n    70\t    chunk_id text PRIMARY KEY, doc_id text NOT NULL, source text NOT NULL,\n    71\t    added_at timestamptz NOT NULL DEFAULT now(), added_by text NOT NULL DEFAULT current_user,\n    72\t    trust text NOT NULL CHECK (trust IN ('reviewed', 'hr_authored')),\n    73\t    audience text NOT NULL CHECK (audience IN ('all', 'employee')),\n    74\t    allowed_employees text[] NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n    75\t    expires_at timestamptz, quarantined boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false, text text NOT NULL,\n    76\t    tsv tsvector GENERATED ALWAYS AS (to_tsvector('english', text)) STORED\n    77\t);\n    78\tCREATE INDEX ON retrieval.chunks USING gin (tsv);\n    79\t\n    80\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit, control, approvals, quota, retrieval TO hr_agent;\n    81\tGRANT INSERT ON audit.events TO hr_agent;\n    82\tGRANT SELECT ON control.stop_flags TO hr_agent;\n    83\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT ON approvals.grants TO hr_agent;\n    84\tGRANT UPDATE (approved_by, approved_at, used_at) ON approvals.grants TO hr_agent;\n    85\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON quota.usage TO hr_agent;\n    86\tGRANT SELECT ON retrieval.chunks, retrieval.index_state TO hr_agent;\n    87\t\n    88\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit, control TO hr_gateway;\n    89\tGRANT INSERT ON audit.gateway_decisions TO hr_gateway;\n    90\tGRANT SELECT ON control.stop_flags TO hr_gateway;\n    91\t\n    92\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA control TO hr_agent_operator;\n    93\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON control.stop_flags TO hr_agent_operator;\n    94\tGRANT USAGE ON SEQUENCE control.stop_flags_flag_id_seq TO hr_agent_operator;\n    95\t\n    96\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA audit TO hr_audit_reader, hr_audit_maint;\n    97\tGRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN SCHEMA audit TO hr_audit_reader;\n    98\tREVOKE EXECUTE ON FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(regclass, interval, int, int) FROM PUBLIC;\n    99\tGRANT EXECUTE ON FUNCTION audit.maintain_partitions(regclass, interval, int, int) TO hr_audit_maint;\n   100\t\n   101\tGRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA retrieval TO hr_docs_ingest;\n   102\tGRANT SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE ON retrieval.chunks, retrieval.index_state TO hr_docs_ingest;\n     1\t\"\"\"Checks applied to content before the model sees it, and to model output.\"\"\"\n     2\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n     3\t\n     4\timport json\n     5\timport re\n     6\timport unicodedata\n     7\tfrom typing import Any\n     8\tfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n     9\t\n    10\tfrom jsonschema import Draft202012Validator, FormatChecker\n    11\t\n    12\tfrom .redact import redact_obj\n    13\tfrom .tools import ToolSpec\n    14\t\n    15\t_INJECTION_MARKERS = [\n    16\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\bignore (all|any|the)? ?(previous|prior|above) (instructions|rules)\"),\n    17\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\byou are now\\b\"),\n    18\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\bsystem prompt\\b\"),\n    19\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)<\\s*/?\\s*(system|assistant|tool_use|instructions)\\b\"),\n    20\t    re.compile(r\"(?i)\\b(call|use|invoke) the [a-z_]+ tool\\b\"),\n    21\t    re.compile(r\"[A-Za-z0-9+/]{120,}={0,2}\"),\n    22\t]\n    23\t\n    24\t\n    25\tclass ValidationRejected(Exception):\n    26\t    def __init__(self, reason: str):\n    27\t        super().__init__(reason)\n    28\t        self.reason = reason\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\tdef _scan_text(value: str, where: str) -> None:\n    32\t    for ch in value:\n    33\t        cat = unicodedata.category(ch)\n    34\t        if cat in (\"Cf\", \"Co\", \"Cs\") or (cat == \"Cc\" and ch not in \"\\n\\t\"):\n    35\t            raise ValidationRejected(f\"{where}: control or invisible character\")\n    36\t    for marker in _INJECTION_MARKERS:\n    37\t        if marker.search(value):\n    38\t            raise ValidationRejected(f\"{where}: instruction-like content\")\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\tdef _walk_strings(value: Any, where: str) -> None:\n    42\t    if isinstance(value, str):\n    43\t        _scan_text(value, where)\n    44\t    elif isinstance(value, dict):\n    45\t        for k, v in value.items():\n    46\t            _walk_strings(v, f\"{where}.{k}\")\n    47\t    elif isinstance(value, list):\n    48\t        for i, v in enumerate(value):\n    49\t            _walk_strings(v, f\"{where}[{i}]\")\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef validate_tool_args(spec: ToolSpec, args: Any) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    53\t    if not isinstance(args, dict):\n    54\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"arguments must be an object\")\n    55\t    errors = sorted(Draft202012Validator(spec.input_schema, format_checker=FormatChecker()).iter_errors(args), key=str)\n    56\t    if errors:\n    57\t        raise ValidationRejected(f\"argument schema: {errors[0].message}\")\n    58\t    return args\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef validate_tool_output(spec: ToolSpec, payload: Any, max_bytes: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    62\t    \"\"\"Type, size, schema and content checks. Any failure rejects the payload.\"\"\"\n    63\t    if spec.output_schema is None:\n    64\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"no output schema configured\")\n    65\t    encoded = json.dumps(payload, ensure_ascii=False)\n    66\t    if len(encoded.encode()) > max_bytes:\n    67\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"output too large\")\n    68\t    if not isinstance(payload, dict):\n    69\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"output must be an object\")\n    70\t    errors = list(Draft202012Validator(spec.output_schema, format_checker=FormatChecker()).iter_errors(payload))\n    71\t    if errors:\n    72\t        raise ValidationRejected(f\"output schema: {errors[0].message}\")\n    73\t    _walk_strings(payload, spec.qualified)\n    74\t    return redact_obj(payload)\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef validate_chunk(chunk: dict[str, Any], max_chars: int) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    78\t    text = chunk[\"text\"]\n    79\t    if not isinstance(text, str) or len(text) > max_chars:\n    80\t        raise ValidationRejected(\"chunk size\")\n    81\t    _walk_strings(text, f\"chunk:{chunk['chunk_id']}\")\n    82\t    return {\n    83\t        \"chunk_id\": chunk[\"chunk_id\"],\n    84\t        \"source\": chunk[\"source\"],\n    85\t        \"trust\": chunk[\"trust\"],\n    86\t        \"text\": redact_obj(text),\n    87\t    }\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t_MD_IMAGE = re.compile(r\"!\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\([^)]*\\)\")\n    91\t_MD_LINK = re.compile(r\"\\[([^\\]]*)\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)[^)]*\\)\")\n    92\t_BARE_URL = re.compile(r\"https?://[^\\s)>\\]]+\")\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tdef sanitize_reply(text: str, allowed_hosts: list[str]) -> str:\n    96\t    \"\"\"Strip images and links to hosts outside the allowlist before the chat client renders them.\"\"\"\n    97\t    text = _MD_IMAGE.sub(\"[image removed]\", text)\n    98\t\n    99\t    def _link(m: re.Match[str]) -> str:\n   100\t        host = urlparse(m.group(2)).hostname or \"\"\n   101\t        return m.group(0) if host in allowed_hosts else m.group(1)\n   102\t\n   103\t    text = _MD_LINK.sub(_link, text)\n   104\t\n   105\t    def _bare(m: re.Match[str]) -> str:\n   106\t        host = urlparse(m.group(0)).hostname or \"\"\n   107\t        return m.group(0) if host in allowed_hosts else \"[link removed]\"\n   108\t\n   109\t    return _BARE_URL.sub(_bare, text)\nsrc/credentials.py:68:    def drop_subject(self, subject: str) -> None:\nk8s/deployment.yaml:60:            capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nk8s/deployment.yaml:113:            capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nk8s/audit-maintenance.yaml:44:                capabilities: {drop: [ALL]}\nrelease/manifest.yaml:79:  retention: 6 months","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0141PFuh1L1eMm4qnqVkZdm4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
