{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFzScrDzU8edgAc5cHbE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B01–B05 and saved the results to `agent/brace-findings.json`. I did not run the `--batch --before-challenges` validation, as you asked. The only checks on the file are the quote checks `answer.py` does when it saves each answer. I did not run challenges, falsification attempts, the topology step or pre-scan resolution. None of the 20 pre-scan hits belong to B01–B05.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B01 | likely_pass | One fixed four-tool allowlist in `config/tools.yaml`. Dispatch is by exact name. MCP tool discovery only feeds a fingerprint comparison; the model never sees discovered tools. No file tools exist. |\n| B02 | needs_evidence | B02.1, B02.2 and B02.4 are yes. B02.3 is unknown because the HRIS and helpdesk MCP servers' audience checks are outside this repo. |\n| B03 | needs_evidence | B03.3 is yes (no secrets checked in). B03.1, B03.2 and B03.4 are unknown. `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `DATABASE_URL` are static Kubernetes Secrets with no rotation recorded, and holder binding downstream can't be judged from here. |\n| B04 | **gap** | If the gateway is unreachable, `escalate_to_human` goes straight to the helpdesk MCP server (`src/gateway_client.py:52-59`, `config/tools.yaml:91-93`). The agent's network policy allows that route (`k8s/networkpolicy.yaml:48-50`). On that path the only stop-flag check runs inside the agent, and the minted token lives 300 s against a 10 s stop target. That fails B04.2 and B04.3. |\n| B05 | likely_pass | Both write tools need an approval from the employee. The approval is bound to operation, target and argument hash, is consumed once, and expires. The agent has no delete, shell or payment tool, and no audit-delete path. |\n\nB01 and B05 are unchallenged, so they don't count as passes yet.\n\nTwo things for later batches:\n- **R04:** `src/retrieval.py:40-49` caches handbook search results by query only, not by employee. One employee's employee-only documents can be served to another. The skill's red-flag list assigns this to R04, so I left it out of B02.\n- **Audit retention:** `KEEP_PARTITIONS=6` in `k8s/audit-maintenance.yaml` with weekly partitions keeps about 6 weeks. The README and `release/manifest.yaml` say 6 months. This is outside B01–B05.\n\nScratch files are in `work/`. Pre-scan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":271,"cache_read_input_tokens":113167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":271},"output_tokens":783,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca543b1a-4cf7-4416-b4c0-b3437adb0361","uuid":"bbd019cb-74c0-455c-b012-3cc57635e44f","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:26:02.546Z","request_id":"req_011ChFzScf4yGFvMqUeG8RrY"}
